Today, GitHub Copilot can take a request in plain language and carry it out for you — in your editor, terminal, desktop application or in the cloud while you focus on something else. We''ve moved from autocomplete to autopilot.

This 3-hours deep dive is built around live demos and real projects. Step by step, we''ll see the many places where AI can help across your workflow: writing and understanding code in the IDE, CLI, and in the Copilot App — then moving into the software delivery lifecycle with PR review, feature creation using cloud agents, and security.

You''ll also learn how to customize Copilot for your own projects and needs, using Skills, Agents, and MCP to connect it to your tools, data, and conventions — and how to automate real work with agentic workflows in plain language, across several languages and tools.

You''ll leave with more than a "wow": concrete techniques to improve quality, control cost, and set the right guardrails, administration, and governance. Expect many demonstrations and plenty of Q&A.

What you''ll learn:

Using Copilot across the IDE, CLI, App and cloud

AI in the SDLC: PR review, cloud agents, and security

Customizing with agents, skills, and custom instructions

Automating tasks with agentic workflows

Improving quality and controlling cost

Guardrails, administration, and governance for teams','{"id": "240e10ff220741eaa5f415aeae5bbd89", "room": "TBA 5", "title": "From Autocomplete to Autopilot: How AI Is Changing the Developer Experience", "endsAt": 1791196200000, "category": "[Deep Dive, INTERMEDIATE, Agentic Engineering & Tooling]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Tugdual Grall]", "startsAt": 1791185400000, "phaseOfDay": "MORNING", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-05", "durationMinutes": 180, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-05T12:30:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-05T09:30:00"}'),
