0074768066,-0.038269043,-0.07019043,0.0018596649,0.017333984,-0.011100769,0.022033691,-0.011444092,-0.018447876,-0.019073486,-0.0003144741,0.042938232,0.02619934,0.013137817,-0.003326416,0.006465912,-0.008163452,-0.01360321,0.013397217,0.008033752,0.008079529,0.047576904,0.005302429,-0.0053634644,-0.022659302,0.0006990433,0.021987915,-0.0008201599,-0.0036773682,0.0074005127,-0.003408432,0.03366089,0.0079574585,-0.008148193,-0.029006958,0.013595581,0.013191223,0.010383606,0.007423401,0.004714966,0.032958984,-0.0030555725,-0.011772156,0.012886047,0.046783447,-0.0051231384,0.029144287,-0.027633667,0.044677734,-0.0041236877,0.02357483,-0.039367676,-0.01171875,0.02003479,-0.0038280487,-0.003484726,-0.006214142,-0.010147095,0.0020008087,-0.0015707016,-0.028198242,0.047821045,-0.0018844604,0.020050049,-0.006969452,0.014694214,-0.0023937225,0.02696228,-0.0016622543,0.01889038,-0.028656006,-0.028167725,0.012023926,-0.010673523,0.0074157715,0.03955078,-0.022567749,-0.004650116,-0.034729004,0.006313324,-0.005004883,0.050628662,-0.0050315857,0.013999939,0.009292603,-0.004081726,-0.023391724,-0.018173218,0.01499176,-0.0039367676,-0.017303467,-0.03439331,-0.012252808,-0.012687683,-0.011886597,-0.003835678,0.02935791,-0.027755737,0.019927979,0.01725769,-0.0053520203,-0.014755249,-0.024917603,-0.0017337799,-0.018554688]'::public.vector,'title:Can AI Build a Jakarta EE Runtime? The Vidocq Experiment, description:This conference started in 2001 as Javapolis, the same year J2EE''s first specs were taking shape. Twenty-five years later, on this stage, we''re closing that loop: implementing those specs with a 2026 AI coding agent as co-author, live.
Part 1 — Building Vidocq, then building something new, live. We''ll walk through how Vidocq, our Jakarta EE Core Profile 11 and MicroProfile 7.1 runtime, came together: the choice to code against formal specifications rather than our own assumptions, and what changed once AI joined that process. Where AI-generated code passed our review but failed spec conformance. Where a spec''s edge cases caught something the AI happily hallucinated past. The workflow we landed on to keep AI output honest against TCK-level requirements. Then we''ll do it live: implementing a Jakarta EE or MicroProfile spec we haven''t built yet, on stage, with an AI agent constrained by the spec text. Real live coding, backup video included in case it goes sideways.
Part 2 — Vidocq, from spec to CLI. A fast tour of what defines the runtime: JPMS enforced at unit granularity, Build Compatible Extensions, and the JDK 25 features (virtual threads, structured concurrency, scoped values) behind Vidocq''s zero external dependencies. Then straight to the command line: we''ll bootstrap and build a small app on Vidocq live, showing how those choices feel to work with, not just how they look in a diagram.
Two decades of spec work, one AI model, one CLI. Watch the gap close.','{"id": "ff291ae00c6e4cce9ea9c2c749c60964", "room": "TBA 2", "title": "Can AI Build a Jakarta EE Runtime? The Vidocq Experiment", "endsAt": 1791210600000, "category": "[Deep Dive, BEGINNER, Agentic Engineering & Tooling]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Antoine Sabot-Durand, yann Blazart, Sebastien Blanc]", "startsAt": 1791199800000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-05", "durationMinutes": 180, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-05T16:30:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-05T13:30:00"}'),
