pattern matching and Data-Oriented Programming

virtual threads and structured concurrency

an on-ramp for beginners and better experiments for experts

new APIs, from stream gatherers to sequenced collections, from lazy constants to HTTP/3

improved performance, like ahead-of-time computation and compact object headers

better security and tooling - most out of the box, some on demand

And there’ll even be time to take a peak at the future and look into the current proposals for value types and string templates, deconstructible class and “withers”. After this deep dive, you’ll be ready to get the most out of the latest Java versions - or at least have good arguments to convince your tech lead to update.','{"id": "7276a7928e1c43a890ccc35d7ac44e62", "room": "TBA 3", "title": "Modern Java in Practice - The Features That Matter", "endsAt": 1791210600000, "category": "[Deep Dive, INTERMEDIATE, Java Language & Platform]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Nicolai Parlog, Falk Sippach]", "startsAt": 1791199800000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-05", "durationMinutes": 180, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-05T16:30:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-05T13:30:00"}'),
