We will build a business application from scratch, and also learn how to work on brownfield projects. We write specifications, let an AI agent generate the code, run it, and add tests that check the code against the spec. When the requirements change, we update the spec and regenerate the code rather than patching the code by hand.

We will explore the harness: the rules, context, and tests around the agent that keep its output predictable enough for real work. By the end, you will know what Spec-Driven Development is, where it helps, where it does not, and how to try it on your own stack.','{"id": "5cebddda92eb40f281ecd24f2044ae28", "room": "TBA 5", "title": "From Developer to Builder: A Spec-Driven Development Deep Dive", "endsAt": 1791210600000, "category": "[Deep Dive, INTERMEDIATE, Agentic Engineering & Tooling]", "dayIndex": 1, "speakers": "[Simon Martinelli]", "startsAt": 1791199800000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-05", "durationMinutes": 180, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-05T16:30:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-05T13:30:00"}'),
