1,-0.02003479,0.009979248,0.01675415,-0.056121826,-0.03741455,-0.0058021545,0.020401001,-0.032440186,0.014762878,0.010894775,0.0013694763,0.0049552917,0.03765869,0.04626465,-0.00024485588,0.0065612793,0.015899658,0.022537231,-0.009887695,-0.0069007874,0.01651001,-0.0010547638,0.012413025,0.045410156,0.0107803345,0.040161133,-0.016540527,-0.035186768,0.018188477,-0.0037231445,-0.0059051514,-0.007183075,0.014289856,0.01939392,-0.013259888,-0.01826477,-0.032104492,0.009552002,0.0135269165,0.013671875,0.0061683655,-0.005027771,0.07067871,0.012168884,-0.008766174,0.024276733,0.032196045,-0.03527832,0.015640259,-0.01121521,0.022567749,-0.027893066,0.037261963,0.003967285,-0.0033168793,0.023284912,0.020965576,0.005065918,-0.03277588,-0.023880005,-0.011444092,0.015380859,-0.009864807,0.051849365,-0.0042877197,0.0048332214,-0.011131287,0.0073509216,0.013282776,0.027008057,-0.0024204254,0.008872986,-0.023712158,0.0031433105,-0.015823364,-0.01838684,-0.015487671,0.027038574,-0.02128601,-0.024520874,0.005088806,-0.017425537,-0.017684937,0.038085938,0.02798462,0.0010681152,0.028701782,0.0073432922,-0.008842468,-0.016342163,-0.013374329,-0.020080566,-0.017227173,-0.03213501,-0.013069153,0.012519836,-0.03756714,-0.03778076,0.011871338,-0.028381348,-0.0064468384,0.028244019,0.014259338,3.8027763e-05,-0.043151855,0.0104522705,-0.029037476]'::public.vector,'title:From Developer to Story Builder: Engineering a Novel, an ARG, and a Transmedia World with AI, description:What happens when a software architect treats a novel like a production system?

In this talk, I will share how I built The Human Protocol, a cyber-realist techno-thriller about AI, using the same engineering principles I apply to software architecture: context engineering, spec-driven development, harness design, versioning, review loops, and automated publishing pipelines.

The session is not about “asking ChatGPT to write a book.” It is a technical case study in designing a controlled human-AI creative workflow. I will show how I created a lore-as-code repository, a governance package to prevent context drift, specialized AI roles for design, drafting and review, and a DevOps-style pipeline to produce manuscript formats for publication.

I will also cover the project’s transmedia extension: an ARG website where clues hidden in the book unlock in-universe content. This was built through spec-driven development anchored in the same lore repository, turning the manuscript into both a story and an interactive system.

You will leave with practical patterns for managing long-running AI-assisted projects: how to structure context, debug hallucinations and inconsistencies, separate agent roles, preserve human intent, and ship complex creative artifacts with AI without losing authorship.','{"id": "97db017ad03044acadfc3977b34d2422", "room": "TBA 2", "title": "From Developer to Story Builder: Engineering a Novel, an ARG, and a Transmedia World with AI", "endsAt": 1791285600000, "category": "[Lunch Talk, BEGINNER, Mind the Geek]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Raphael Semeteys]", "startsAt": 1791283200000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-06", "durationMinutes": 40, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-06T13:20:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-06T12:40:00"}'),
