20492554,-0.008987427,0.005012512,-0.034729004,-0.036346436,-0.00022494793,-0.01033783,-0.00945282,-0.041412354,0.01146698,0.01235199,-0.01977539,0.011421204,-0.014823914,-0.025405884,0.02494812,0.031829834,0.04711914,0.0021591187,0.021392822,-0.022705078,-0.0029449463,0.0128479,-0.023132324,-0.005935669,0.0066375732,0.005104065,0.029846191,0.017791748,0.0007967949,-0.016143799,-0.048065186,0.037261963,0.017440796,-0.045043945,0.010383606,0.0004117489,-0.0020179749,-0.009490967,-0.0031661987,-0.01625061,0.013793945,0.015289307,0.016525269,-0.026428223,0.020111084,0.059326172,-0.012557983,-0.018493652,-0.016906738,0.019729614,-0.039733887,0.0309906,-0.016433716,0.037841797,0.00157547,0.04055786,0.019927979,-0.002954483,0.0023403168,0.017944336,0.011581421,-0.014091492,0.0052833557,-0.011772156,0.014373779,-0.015686035,0.039489746,0.021820068,0.03656006,0.0041275024,0.020492554,0.006587982,0.01108551,-0.021133423,0.008125305,-0.007171631,0.011985779,0.011642456,-0.00374794,-0.005710602,0.0057029724,-0.008987427,-0.03152466,-0.028671265,-0.010787964,-0.011413574,0.058258057,0.02760315,-0.021972656,0.012893677,0.026382446,-0.016586304,-0.024047852,-0.0050468445,0.0029659271,-0.019317627,-0.016616821,-0.0056915283,0.013023376,-0.0055236816,-0.02658081,0.033477783,-0.031311035,0.032714844,0.023269653,-0.01852417,-0.018859863,0.0051612854,-0.010284424,-0.012908936]'::public.vector,'title:Beyond system.out.println: Applying a Debugging Mindset at Scale, description:Debugging a consistently failing unit test is easy; you set a breakpoint and fix it. But how do you debug a "random" failure in a massive microservices landscape or a distributed monolith?

During an interview, I was once told, "You are more of a debugger than a coder." They were right: I thrive on the bugs that make others give up: the nasty, intermittent issues hidden under the carpet.
But you cannot solve these issues with ''System.out.println()'' or a simple debugger attached to localhost.

Debugging at scale requires a shift in mindset and tooling. It requires moving from the paradigm of "5 Whys" and ''logger.info'' to a structured observational approach based on observability data.
Based on production outages, I''ll share how I uncovered the problems, the lessons I learned and how you can combine a debugging mindset with observability tooling like OpenTelemetry and the Grafana toolset to gain deeper insights.','{"id": "346816f0261948cda312a9aea46edad6", "room": "TBA 3", "title": "Beyond system.out.println: Applying a Debugging Mindset at Scale", "endsAt": 1791285600000, "category": "[Lunch Talk, BEGINNER, Development Practices]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Cees Bos]", "startsAt": 1791283200000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-06", "durationMinutes": 40, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-06T13:20:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-06T12:40:00"}'),
