From its beginnings at Sun Microsystems to OpenJDK, the JVM ecosystem, and the transition from Java EE to Jakarta EE, this documentary traces 31 years of innovation, disruption, reinvention, and community.

The story is told by the people who shaped it, including James Gosling, Joshua Bloch, James Duncan Davidson, Tim Lindholm, Kim Polese, Carla Schroer, Sharat Chander, and many others.

Through their memories and perspectives, we revisit the decisions, breakthroughs, challenges, and communities that turned Java into one of the most influential software platforms ever created.

Thirty-one years later, Java is still here—not just because of the technology, but because generations of people decided it was worth carrying forward.','{"id": "bb3754a9f5bd4d84b2b420127d242b5a", "room": "TBA 6", "title": "The Java Story | The Official Documentary", "endsAt": 1791305400000, "category": "[Documentary, BEGINNER, Java Language & Platform]", "dayIndex": 2, "speakers": "[Georges Saab]", "startsAt": 1791300900000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-06", "durationMinutes": 75, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-06T18:50:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-06T17:35:00"}'),
