5675,-0.017211914,0.020111084,-0.012451172,-0.03164673,-0.0013751984,0.037506104,-0.026489258,-0.0073928833,-0.01285553,-0.0074386597,-0.003129959,0.008522034,0.050750732,0.014228821,0.019058228,-0.015060425,0.010192871,0.0019311905,-0.01838684,0.00033807755,0.019500732,0.010276794,0.052764893,-0.010314941,0.01876831,-0.017669678,-0.020202637,0.014350891,0.003030777,-0.020217896,-0.026123047,0.005657196,0.017562866,-0.014434814,-0.029693604,-0.032318115,0.010528564,0.01474762,0.004131317,0.01902771,-0.0061798096,0.048187256,0.0049095154,-0.01473999,-0.0054893494,0.046020508,-0.03427124,0.019882202,-0.013458252,0.03250122,-0.01574707,0.04663086,0.02178955,0.02027893,0.0018844604,0.024765015,-0.008644104,-0.019973755,-0.012832642,-0.007888794,0.009483337,-0.015792847,0.03201294,0.03918457,0.029388428,-0.022445679,0.011405945,0.002128601,0.02444458,-0.0027599335,0.009552002,-0.023040771,-0.015159607,0.017974854,0.012939453,-0.010826111,0.012031555,-0.029632568,-0.025558472,-0.0418396,0.012458801,-0.01663208,0.052612305,0.038635254,-0.011955261,-0.01398468,0.01789856,-0.035583496,-0.039398193,0.014732361,-0.008255005,-0.017059326,-0.026947021,-0.015731812,0.025039673,-0.013656616,-0.042175293,0.027954102,-0.042785645,0.01361084,0.01864624,0.0143585205,0.0012588501,-0.03540039,-0.010520935,-0.029556274]'::public.vector,'title:A Fleet of AI Agents, Each in Its Own Sandbox: Inside Docker''s Agentic Platform, description:What if your next pull request was opened by an AI agent, one that read the issue, wrote the code, ran the tests, and only pinged you when it was ready to merge?

That''s how Docker''s engineering team ships software today. Built on top of Docker Cloud Sandboxes, the Docker Agentic Platform gives every AI agent its own isolated environment: real shell access, a live Docker daemon, git, GitHub CLI, and a JWT-scoped identity. Orchestrators spawn specialists, architect, implementer, reviewer ; that work in parallel across sandboxed boundaries, coordinating asynchronously without ever touching each other''s secrets or state.

We''ll walk the hard lessons (context cost, hallucinations, knowing when to keep a human in the loop), and what it takes to make autonomous agents safe and observable in production.','{"id": "92ce0dce07314b6f8c11fcdd781750d5", "room": "TBA 7", "title": "A Fleet of AI Agents, Each in Its Own Sandbox: Inside Docker''s Agentic Platform", "endsAt": 1791363000000, "category": "[Keynote, INTERMEDIATE, Agentic Engineering & Tooling]", "dayIndex": 3, "speakers": "[Jean-Laurent de Morlhon]", "startsAt": 1791361800000, "phaseOfDay": "MORNING", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-07", "durationMinutes": 20, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T10:50:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T10:30:00"}'),
