2,-0.039855957,-0.0011234283,0.021591187,-0.04159546,0.03692627,-0.0013217926,-0.023406982,-0.010299683,0.019470215,0.07470703,0.020553589,-0.018722534,-0.00066518784,-0.015579224,0.01637268,-0.020935059,-0.009773254,-0.0082473755,0.008865356,0.038726807,0.007820129,-0.008148193,-0.02192688,-0.03414917,0.031219482,-0.005279541,-0.019683838,0.011169434,0.0107421875,0.005493164,-0.011199951,-0.002401352,-0.038848877,0.012229919,-0.012367249,0.012084961,0.004627228,-0.0021839142,0.04019165,-0.020965576,-0.013572693,-0.012145996,0.034698486,-0.02848816,0.021255493,0.0006365776,0.015052795,-0.033599854,0.038391113,-0.0047340393,0.021942139,-0.0015716553,0.026824951,0.012886047,0.018600464,0.014007568,-0.0027103424,0.0024261475,-0.010749817,0.028625488,0.044006348,0.030273438,-0.0007958412,0.029266357,-0.0003142357,0.009521484,-0.035461426,-0.009979248,0.02078247,-0.0030460358,0.016998291,-0.027404785,0.010353088,0.004486084,-0.01876831,-0.025238037,-0.005771637,0.009025574,-0.0008635521,0.041900635,0.013305664,-0.01864624,0.037872314,0.000828743,-0.020690918,-0.020355225,-0.011428833,-0.0049972534,-0.0070533752,-0.021560669,0.014816284,0.019805908,-0.030227661,-0.024139404,0.041625977,-0.022567749,0.0047798157,0.033996582,-0.0074386597,-0.0030002594,-0.032806396,-0.014694214,-0.057403564]'::public.vector,'title:Emergent DevEx: The Good, the Bad, and the Legacy, description:What happens when an organization grows from a few co-founders into 10,000 people?

In a big organization, the developer experience isn''t something you sit down and design. It''s the sum of countless small changes, layered year after year. It emerges slowly, pulled in different directions by three forces:

the dead weight of history, baked into bureaucratic processes and controls;

the endless transformation projects that promise heaven but just swap one mess for another;

and the developers stuck in the middle, bearing the pressure.

Through real-life scenarios, we''ll show how small changes to implementation, not grand top-down strategy, are often what make a developer''s life easier.

Key Takeaways:

How developer experience grows alongside an organization, from a team of 5 to 10,000+.

How history, transformation efforts, and developers themselves each leave their mark.

What internal developer communities can do to shift things and how, even as one developer, you can change the details for the greater good.','{"id": "8ad050808ea14c96bd558560e7cf562e", "room": "TBA 3", "title": "Emergent DevEx: The Good, the Bad, and the Legacy", "endsAt": 1791370200000, "category": "[Conference, BEGINNER, People, Practices & Career]", "dayIndex": 3, "speakers": "[Makan Sepehrifar, Soroosh Khodami]", "startsAt": 1791367200000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-07", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T12:50:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T12:00:00"}'),
