* how classical RSA encryption works
* how quantum algorithms (i.e. Shor’s algorithm) break RSA
* brief overview of where we are regarding quantum hardware
* why PQC still matters right now, to prevent “harvest now, decrypt later” attacks
* what lattice-based PQC looks like and how far along we already are in adopting it

The target audience is everyone generally interested in future technologies. Especially everyone who might have heard about quantum computing and Shor''s algorithm breaking encryption, but don''t know what that means for the future of cryptography and where we''re at today.

The key take aways are a (very basic) general understanding how quantum computing works, to understand how it has the potential to break RSA, as well as quantum-safe encryption methods that are already being put in place, how they work and what the future might look like.','{"id": "58714df33c514dc49d52ece212f98a64", "room": "TBA 6", "title": "Post-Quantum Today: How Your Passwords Will Be Safe in a Quantum Future", "endsAt": 1791370200000, "category": "[Conference, ADVANCED, Security, Trust & Compliance]", "dayIndex": 3, "speakers": "[Julian Burr]", "startsAt": 1791367200000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-07", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T12:50:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T12:00:00"}'),
