We have on one hand, standard APIs with Ingress, Service of type: LoadBalancer, and even NodePords…
And in the other hand, some proprietary APIs, from Ingress controllers or Services meshes… more advanced, but not standard 😅.

After so many years of solution and confusion, a new API, named GatewayAPI, arise to solve these problems for developers, cluster & infrastructure operators 🤯!

We''ll discover together this new API, standard and advanced features, implementations available and of course, how to install it in your cluster ⚡️','{"id": "088c379aa7004fdab6e5c64b1ad45744", "room": "TBA 9", "title": "🌉 Gateway API, 10 years of maturation for a new Kubernetes network API", "endsAt": 1791377400000, "category": "[Conference, INTERMEDIATE, Cloud Native, Data & Infrastructure]", "dayIndex": 3, "speakers": "[Kevin Davin]", "startsAt": 1791374400000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-07", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T14:50:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T14:00:00"}'),
