8178711,-0.018295288,-0.049102783,0.020751953,0.03463745,-0.0206604,0.014907837,0.010513306,-0.01600647,0.014427185,0.015991211,0.06286621,0.03817749,-8.690357e-05,-0.012870789,0.019607544,0.01777649,-0.018249512,-0.011489868,-0.01725769,0.011260986,0.052703857,-0.0009918213,0.028030396,-0.0035095215,-0.020477295,0.03012085,1.1444092e-05,-0.018981934,0.025131226,0.0018100739,0.008155823,0.0009703636,0.00299263,-0.017440796,0.000957489,0.009086609,0.008117676,0.0034999847,0.019882202,0.059387207,0.0076026917,-0.031341553,0.00907135,0.021057129,-0.029693604,0.020553589,-0.014862061,0.039398193,-0.014907837,0.030181885,-0.0071983337,0.014709473,0.0025348663,0.020950317,0.005050659,0.025131226,-0.00055646896,0.010650635,0.006504059,-0.011619568,0.038360596,0.03970337,0.029785156,0.0022678375,0.015090942,0.00969696,0.0236969,-0.025543213,0.007675171,-0.027694702,0.001917839,0.016967773,-0.013084412,0.0060157776,0.023117065,-0.029815674,-0.03074646,-0.00957489,-0.020858765,-0.030212402,0.036956787,0.006767273,0.017700195,0.006008148,-0.017364502,-0.031951904,-0.0073127747,-0.0033569336,0.009719849,-0.008712769,-0.03955078,-0.0052833557,0.03579712,-0.028396606,-0.008071899,0.04284668,-0.031341553,0.00957489,0.036865234,0.017349243,-0.020751953,-0.030761719,0.0058555603,-0.026367188]'::public.vector,'title:How to survive and thrive as a dev (team) in the exponential age of AI. Real-world AI adoption, smarter ways of working, and lessons from the front lines, description:The AI revolution isn’t coming — it’s already altering how we architect products, ship features, and run engineering teams.

During this talk, in his signature charismatic style, Sander Hoogendoorn, CTO at iBOOD.com and a seasoned developer with over four decades of coding experience, doesn’t get stuck in theory or hype, but confronts the pressing issues head-on. You’ll get a no-fluff, grounded view from iBOOD — what we’re already doing with AI, how we built it into our systems, and how it shapes the way we work.

We won’t shy away from the dark side either — vendor lock-in, breaking prompts, model opacity, shifting APIs, and how quickly a dependency can become fragile. These are real risks that shape architectural and organizational decisions we make daily.

To survive exponential speed, we retired many practices: no Scrum, no rigid ceremonies, no big upfront plans, no pull requests or code reviews. Instead, we embrace working in fluid autonomous microteams, continuous learning, experimentation, and radical adaptability.

Expect an honest, fast-paced, and experience-driven session — mixing architecture, culture, and practical insight — on what it truly takes for developers and teams to survive and thrive in the age of AI.','{"id": "6b81396181d54039998f5c5dd6a037b3", "room": "TBA 8", "title": "How to survive and thrive as a dev (team) in the exponential age of AI. Real-world AI adoption, smarter ways of working, and lessons from the front lines", "endsAt": 1791381600000, "category": "[Conference, INTERMEDIATE, Agentic Engineering & Tooling]", "dayIndex": 3, "speakers": "[Sander Hoogendoorn]", "startsAt": 1791378600000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-07", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T16:00:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T15:10:00"}'),
