This talk covers the patterns that prevent that chaos: the Dual Write problem, Outbox and Inbox patterns for consistency between database and event stream, idempotent consumers, and Sagas — Orchestration and Choreography.

You''ll leave knowing which pattern solves which problem, when to use each, and what you''re really trading off with eventual consistency','{"id": "9a84417ee3834e3f83a51d4f2345523f", "room": "TBA 4", "title": "Consistency Patterns in Event-Driven Architecture", "endsAt": 1791387000000, "category": "[Conference, INTERMEDIATE, Architecture & Modernization]", "dayIndex": 3, "speakers": "[Emanuel Trandafir]", "startsAt": 1791384000000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-07", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T17:30:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T16:40:00"}'),
