,-0.03640747,0.010002136,0.016326904,-0.017211914,-0.002412796,-0.0022068024,-0.018051147,-0.022888184,0.020721436,0.03555298,-0.0011396408,-0.0146102905,0.0015115738,-0.0027160645,0.0019702911,-0.0037021637,-0.0041160583,0.012084961,0.005558014,0.04437256,-0.006958008,0.0031871796,-0.039489746,-0.03781128,0.03338623,0.011650085,-0.036193848,0.0047302246,-0.01928711,-0.026947021,-0.0038452148,0.0017681122,-0.038360596,0.044555664,0.00749588,0.013549805,-0.0025634766,-0.007167816,0.019607544,0.01776123,0.007762909,0.00013387203,0.025726318,0.01272583,0.013145447,-0.01637268,0.03817749,-0.021270752,-0.0012359619,-0.0090408325,0.026046753,0.019348145,0.032806396,-0.007133484,-0.03744507,-0.0029659271,-0.017501831,0.031555176,0.002954483,0.035949707,-0.02507019,0.018569946,-0.028778076,0.02949524,0.021133423,0.0010652542,0.0025672913,0.04067993,-0.008926392,-0.011383057,0.0053482056,0.016845703,-0.008041382,0.015731812,-0.025238037,0.010574341,-0.013435364,-0.011871338,-0.0019760132,0.024139404,-0.0063438416,0.0014638901,0.029525757,-0.0015563965,-0.013214111,-0.020477295,0.003643036,-0.002866745,-0.007083893,-0.005832672,-0.022598267,-0.0034828186,-0.025909424,-0.03488159,0.0104522705,-0.03010559,0.014892578,0.011016846,0.00081539154,-0.015914917,-0.030532837,-0.01084137,-0.02885437]'::public.vector,'title:GraalVM Next: Layers, Crema, and WebAssembly in Action, description:What if native images could share code and memory, load new classes at run time, and run applications in the browser?

In this session, we’ll explore three projects expanding what GraalVM Native Image can do.

— Native Image Layers introduce a brand-new concept of reusable base images, allowing multiple applications to share code and memory.
— Project Crema adds dynamic class loading and execution to native applications — goodbye, closed world!
— Web Image (experimental) can compile JVM applications to WebAssembly, bringing libraries and applications directly to browsers and other WebAssembly environments.

Each project expands a different aspect of Native Image: how applications are packaged, what happens at run time, and where applications can run.

In this session we’ll see these forward-looking projects in action and discuss where they stand today.','{"id": "ff0fd128a60e4f7fb3db21710ed11c2f", "room": "TBA 5", "title": "GraalVM Next: Layers, Crema, and WebAssembly in Action", "endsAt": 1791387000000, "category": "[Conference, INTERMEDIATE, Development Practices]", "dayIndex": 3, "speakers": "[Alina Yurenko]", "startsAt": 1791384000000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-07", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T17:30:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T16:40:00"}'),
