3943,-0.03640747,-0.010231018,0.00077438354,-0.020553589,-0.02949524,-0.0002655983,0.021377563,-0.03338623,0.04449463,-0.0046043396,0.011299133,0.0058174133,0.02394104,0.030838013,-0.015205383,0.012649536,-0.00459671,0.012313843,0.033935547,0.008987427,0.001739502,0.015434265,0.023986816,0.041534424,-0.019226074,0.032928467,0.0030155182,-0.02444458,0.028182983,0.012283325,-0.027236938,-0.0003786087,0.011512756,0.010528564,-0.0050849915,-0.0016698837,-0.017913818,0.012771606,0.014892578,0.005710602,0.005821228,0.0025730133,0.055999756,-0.0013046265,-0.0096206665,0.009819031,0.027923584,-0.027816772,0.01537323,0.0020599365,0.0078125,-0.024490356,0.028442383,-0.01020813,-0.023086548,0.012901306,0.021392822,0.0042419434,0.009292603,-0.017974854,-0.01979065,0.00554657,-0.0008854866,0.039978027,-0.0005750656,0.017044067,-0.02583313,0.021713257,0.013809204,0.00818634,-0.01637268,-0.0029239655,-0.019882202,-0.013008118,0.026672363,-0.018753052,0.007633209,0.014801025,-0.018676758,-0.01625061,-0.011306763,0.010498047,-0.0206604,0.025665283,0.0137786865,0.008918762,0.023406982,-0.008361816,-0.023345947,-0.010025024,0.016708374,-0.028335571,-0.01940918,-0.010482788,-0.0023269653,0.029891968,-0.030410767,-0.018081665,0.04171753,-0.014801025,0.018966675,0.032958984,0.01828003,0.0019454956,-0.026931763,0.009880066,-0.016906738]'::public.vector,'title:AI Made Building Cheap. Now Decisions Are the Bottleneck., description:AI is transforming software delivery. Code can be generated, tests created, architectures sketched, and implementation options explored in minutes. Building has never been cheaper.
Yet many organisations are discovering an unexpected consequence: as execution accelerates, decision-making becomes the real bottleneck.
Drawing on consulting engagements across banking, insurance, retail, and telecommunications, this talk explores how AI is changing the economics of software delivery and why decision quality is emerging as a competitive advantage. Rather than focusing on generating code faster, I demonstrate how AI can improve discovery, architecture, and delivery conversations before implementation begins.
Through practical examples and live demonstrations, attendees will see how conversations can be transformed into Event Storming maps, Team Topologies views, C4 architecture diagrams, assumptions, risks, and architectural options. These techniques help teams expose hidden complexity, align stakeholders faster, and make better-informed decisions.
Key takeaways: Understand why AI shifts the constraint from execution to judgement, learn practical techniques for AI-assisted discovery and architecture, expose risks and assumptions earlier, and balance delivery speed with architectural integrity.
Target audience: Software architects, technical leads, senior engineers, engineering managers, enterprise architects, and technology leaders.','{"id": "e259d7e8ea0f4d65879b016285cf7988", "room": "TBA 8", "title": "AI Made Building Cheap. Now Decisions Are the Bottleneck.", "endsAt": 1791387000000, "category": "[Conference, ADVANCED, People, Practices & Career]", "dayIndex": 3, "speakers": "[Dave Sammut, João Rosa]", "startsAt": 1791384000000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-07", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T17:30:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T16:40:00"}'),
