tools, point it at your data and watch it do something that felt impossible two years ago. The demo lands well.
Then you try to put it in front of real customers, and the questions start.
Which model are you allowed to use in production? Where do the credentials live now? What stops the agent
from calling a tool it should never touch? What does one conversation cost?
None of this is about the model. It is about the platform underneath it, and it looks a lot like the problem
developers hit when they first tried to ship containers.
This session shows what platform engineering has to offer next. Model access as a paved road, identity for
agents, guardrails you inherit instead of build, and observability that shows every step and what it cost. You will
leave knowing what to ask your platform team for, and if you are the platform team, what to build first.','{"id": "4f8934b9b65e429b9408c1faeaa8021f", "room": "TBA 9", "title": "Building an Agent Ready Platform", "endsAt": 1791387000000, "category": "[Conference, BEGINNER, Agentic Engineering & Tooling]", "dayIndex": 3, "speakers": "[Timo Salm]", "startsAt": 1791384000000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-07", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T17:30:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T16:40:00"}'),
