But developers don''t necessarily want to become Kubernetes specialists.

This presentation will focus on what developers need to know to get the most of Kubernetes without having to become a DevOps.

We will cover:

modern local development environment (flox, kind...)

building container images (multistage build, build without docker...)

important kubernetes features developers need to know and how to handle them efficiently (requests/limits, graceful shutdown, probes, OCI volumes...)

how to investigate and debug code on kubernetes (kubectl debug, mirrord...)

how to secure applications (SecurityContext, CEL, SBOM, RuntimeClass with gVisor/Kata...)

how to integrate observability with OpenTelemetry

The presentation will contain examples and demos with a strong focus on Best Practices.','{"id": "454bbee71df24824bd3512ae29e5bf71", "room": "TBA 4", "title": "Kubernetes for Developers", "endsAt": 1791391200000, "category": "[Conference, INTERMEDIATE, Cloud Native, Data & Infrastructure]", "dayIndex": 3, "speakers": "[Alain Regnier]", "startsAt": 1791388200000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-07", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T18:40:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-07T17:50:00"}'),
