This talk challenges the perception that innovation cannot thrive in highly regulated environments like banking. As engineers working within strict rules and predefined tech stacks, we showcase how AI is actively transforming our daily work. We explore concrete initiatives such as instruction files, agent-based automation, skills-driven architectures, emerging agentic hubs and internal prompt libraries that enhance knowledge sharing. We also highlight how tools like Copilot significantly boost developer productivity.
Beyond enterprise use, we share our involvement in ING’s Devoxx4Kids initiative, where we inspire children aged 7-14 to explore technology. We present two platforms we developed: CodeKids Lab, which teaches programming through playful interaction and Cybersecurity Lab, which raises awareness of digital threats in an engaging way. AI plays a key role in enabling both innovation and education.

Key Takeaways

AI can thrive even in constrained, regulated environments

Tangible gains in developer productivity through AI tooling

AI can extend beyond business value to create social impact

A real example of engineers turning curiosity into meaningful initiatives

Target Audience
This presentation targets software engineers, tech leads and innovation enthusiasts working in regulated industries, as well as developers interested in applied AI. It also appeals to educators and professionals passionate about using IT for social good and inspiring the next generation.','{"id": "597ab40edcf64937a033f7e2f774ea10", "room": "TBA 2", "title": "Rewriting the rules: How AI transforms engineering and inspiring young minds", "endsAt": 1791447600000, "category": "[Conference, BEGINNER, Mind the Geek]", "dayIndex": 4, "speakers": "[Ayoub Hammou Ahabchane, Kamel Zaraoui]", "startsAt": 1791444600000, "phaseOfDay": "MORNING", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-08", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T10:20:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T09:30:00"}'),
