In this session, Martin takes the audience on a journey through the history of developer tools to the present AI inflection point. He will:

Reflect on what human engineers actually need from their environment in 2026.

Analyze whether the IDE is evolving or being replaced by terminal-based workflows like Claude Code.

Discuss the evolving role of AI agents as the new "power users" of development tools.

Summarize the implications for both toolsmiths and software engineers in the years to come.','{"id": "cf3bd9d4e261458ba4c2075a66f68bba", "room": "TBA 7", "title": "Is the IDE dead ?", "endsAt": 1791459300000, "category": "[Lunch Talk, INTERMEDIATE, Agentic Engineering & Tooling]", "dayIndex": 4, "speakers": "[Martin Lippert]", "startsAt": 1791456900000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-08", "durationMinutes": 40, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T13:35:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T12:55:00"}'),
