I will also present reports comparing how different LLM models generate code, showing clear differences in stability, output consistency, and the amount of guidance each model needs to avoid mistakes.

And last but not least, I will talk about the elephant in the room: metrics 📏. How do we measure our improvement using AI? Is it something companies are doing right? Spoiler alert ... no 😰

The talk focuses on helping teams build more reliable, productive, and secure AI workflows, making AI code generation a real benefit rather than a risky experiment 😅.','{"id": "45f54e3fc1c242f7a509d3ffcbbc7071", "room": "TBA 7", "title": "Agents With Seatbelts: Practical Ways to Keep AI Code Gen Under Control", "endsAt": 1791451800000, "category": "[Conference, INTERMEDIATE, Development Practices]", "dayIndex": 4, "speakers": "[Jonathan Vila López]", "startsAt": 1791448800000, "phaseOfDay": "MORNING", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-08", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T11:30:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T10:40:00"}'),
