To address these everyday use cases, a new JEP proposes a simple, incubating API for parsing, navigating, and generating JSON documents-both for Java developers and for the JDK itself.

While the Java ecosystem offers many libraries with JSON-processing capabilities, this built-in API is not intended to replace them, but rather to offer a low-friction option when an external library would be unnecessary or impractical.

In this talk, we will show how Data-Oriented Programming helps simplify the API, discuss its intended use cases, outline the design trade-offs, and demonstrate its capabilities.','{"id": "90a4ed1ef09c47d0a3af7a0bf060c293", "room": "TBA 5", "title": "Everyday JSON", "endsAt": 1791472800000, "category": "[Conference, INTERMEDIATE, Java Language & Platform]", "dayIndex": 4, "speakers": "[Viktor Klang]", "startsAt": 1791469800000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-08", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T17:20:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T16:30:00"}'),
