This session explores real engineering challenges encountered while building PDF technology at scale, from compatibility and performance to security, testing, and interoperability. Through a series of stories and hard-earned lessons, you''ll see why mature systems can be some of the best teachers for designing resilient software and why the hardest problems are often the ones users never notice.','{"id": "f269e5aee6f948599f12a23fa81a05b2", "room": "TBA 2", "title": "Engineering Lessons from Working on Software Older Than Me", "endsAt": 1791459300000, "category": "[Lunch Talk, BEGINNER, Development Practices]", "dayIndex": 4, "speakers": "[Guust Ysebie]", "startsAt": 1791456900000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-08", "durationMinutes": 40, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T13:35:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T12:55:00"}'),
