46,-0.0029964447,-0.034179688,-0.0027332306,0.0040245056,-0.033081055,-0.048187256,0.007484436,0.03289795,-0.019515991,0.025787354,-0.005432129,-0.005455017,0.00617218,0.021270752,0.045074463,0.013259888,0.0011205673,0.00041604042,-0.0023231506,0.011100769,-0.023788452,0.0049209595,0.018218994,0.009742737,0.03463745,-0.009346008,0.028656006,0.0019664764,-0.021591187,0.04360962,0.01789856,-0.012161255,0.0013799667,0.005836487,0.03881836,0.0002872944,-0.011383057,-0.027633667,-0.008674622,0.004558563,0.004798889,0.009727478,0.011398315,0.060028076,0.0027580261,-0.028717041,0.0181427,0.029922485,-0.021270752,0.008407593,-0.0057373047,0.020355225,-0.033355713,0.02784729,-0.008216858,-0.015312195,0.0069122314,0.028900146,0.0031280518,-0.0074691772,-0.010231018,-0.002418518,0.02180481,-0.013648987,0.027648926,0.02571106,0.01979065,0.0011119843,0.0076904297,-0.0019741058,0.015007019,-0.007713318,-0.003145218,-0.01600647,0.0039482117,0.011955261,0.00598526,-0.00881958,0.03050232,-0.0075912476,-0.027359009,-0.00090646744,-0.0022830963,-0.02633667,0.047210693,0.012748718,-0.0034446716,0.029006958,-0.0024852753,-0.025985718,-0.034942627,0.0021915436,-0.015083313,-0.014984131,-0.017150879,-0.007171631,0.02168274,-0.02658081,-0.016403198,0.04095459,-0.026870728,0.013038635,0.019500732,0.0009784698,-0.0132751465,-0.043273926,0.0017280579,-0.032684326]'::public.vector,'title:Software engineering in the age of AI agents: who’s in control?, description:An AI deletes a production database… and insists it didn''t. Welcome to modern software engineering.
95% of developers now use AI tools weekly. Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot - agentic coding assistants are writing more code than ever. But the data shows a darker side: up to 5 times more technical debt, over 40% higher code complexity, and a flood of code that needs review.
The real shift isn''t about writing more code faster. It''s about moving from writing code to writing specs, from building systems to generating them, and from trusting output to verifying it.
In this talk, I''ll share real stories - including a production database incident, a 45-minute spec-to-app demo, and lessons from 3 projects built in 1 hour. You''ll leave with a practical framework: experiment boldly, deploy carefully, and raise the bar on testing. One rule applies no matter what: if you bring it to a review, it''s your code.','{"id": "e920d7ac0f084bc79a093f95d483cfff", "room": "TBA 8", "title": "Software engineering in the age of AI agents: who’s in control?", "endsAt": 1791463200000, "category": "[Conference, INTERMEDIATE, Agentic Engineering & Tooling]", "dayIndex": 4, "speakers": "[Bert Jan Schrijver]", "startsAt": 1791460200000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-08", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T14:40:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T13:50:00"}'),
