In this session, Smals Research shares practical experience from real e-government projects. Through the migration of ageing Java applications from Java EE to Jakarta EE, the speakers explore how AI supports software modernization. Topics include namespace changes, deprecated APIs, outdated dependencies and complex build configurations.

The session highlights where AI genuinely accelerates migration work, where it falls short, and how teams can keep modernization efforts reliable and verifiable. Drawing on additional experience with other legacy environments, including COBOL, the speakers also share practical approaches for documenting, rewriting and maintaining legacy code with AI assistance.

Whether you''re modernizing an existing application or exploring AI-assisted development, this session offers a realistic view of what AI can and cannot do today.','{"id": "d8c068d457a941718c515fa47fcb1c8d", "room": "TBA 2", "title": "Modernizing legacy code with AI: hands-on examples & lessons learned", "endsAt": 1791467400000, "category": "[Conference, BEGINNER, Agentic Engineering & Tooling]", "dayIndex": 4, "speakers": "[Koen Vanderkimpen, Wim Lambrecht]", "startsAt": 1791464400000, "phaseOfDay": "AFTERNOON", "conferenceDay": "2026-10-08", "durationMinutes": 50, "endsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T15:50:00", "startsAtLocalDateTime": "2026-10-08T15:00:00"}'),
